Notes:
  RENAMED to "Homi" ("feel like home") across all user-visible strings, with the supplied
  logo at apps/web/public/homi-logo.png used in the top bar and the printable brief.
  Palette retuned from cobalt to the brand's terracotta/maroon/sand; every token's
  contrast recomputed and documented in tailwind.config.ts. The npm package name
  "@mainhaus/web" was deliberately LEFT ALONE because the root scripts filter on it.

  MAP no longer needs any credential. MapCanvas picks: Google (if browser key) ->
  MapLibre over OpenStreetMap tiles (default, keyless) -> schematic plot (no WebGL).
  Address search: Google Geocoder with a key, OSM Nominatim without (1100 ms debounce
  to respect its rate limit, attribution shown). The brief's condition on a MapLibre
  alternative is enforced in code: tileConfig.isGoogleSourced() withholds Google Places
  records from the non-Google basemap and the map states how many were withheld.

  THREE REAL BUGS found and fixed while testing (not test-only issues):
   1. MapLibre throws without WebGL, and an uncaught render error unmounts the whole
      React tree - the entire app went blank, not just the map. Fixed with a WebGL
      pre-check plus MapErrorBoundary; covered by the new "no-webgl" Playwright project.
   2. The transport probe treated HTTP 200 on /api/health as proof of a backend. Any SPA
      fallback (including `vite preview`) answers with index.html and 200, so the app
      selected the live transport and then failed every call. The probe now requires a
      response that parses as the contract's health envelope.
   3. Result cards said "Sample lease available" for slots still awaiting their document.
      Changed to the truthful "Demo lease slot"; raised CR-11 (additive
      Listing.demoPolicyStatus) so the card can say the stronger thing honestly.

  FOR CODEX:
